title: Role::DependencyCheck bundles set-time and report-time, so json cannot be required
updated: 2026-08-12T01:15:44Z
---

Fallout from #128, filed rather than folded in because it has to touch Cmd::Create and Cmd::Pick.

Role::DependencyCheck now declares `requires qw( store find_task usage_error quiet )`. The fifth call it makes, $self->json in dependency_report, could not go on the list: Cmd::Create composes the whole role for parse_dependency_ids/assert_dependencies_exist alone -- the set-time half -- and has no --json of its own, so requiring json refuses a consumer that never reaches the reporting half:

    Cant apply App::karr::Role::DependencyCheck to App::karr::Cmd::Create
      - missing json at lib/App/karr/Cmd/Create.pm line 15.

So one role carries two concerns with two different contracts:

  set-time    parse_dependency_ids, assert_dependencies_exist
              needs usage_error, find_task
              consumers: Create, Edit

  report-time check_dependencies, dependency_report, _dependency_warnings
              needs store, find_task, json, quiet
              consumers: TaskMutation (and through it Move/Edit/Delete/Archive/Handoff), Pick

Splitting them lets each half declare its own requires in full, and stops Create inheriting two methods it must never call. It changes the `with` line in Cmd::Create, Cmd::Pick and Role::TaskMutation, which is why it is not part of #128.

The alternative -- give create a --json and require json outright -- is a user-visible CLI change and a separate decision.

t/135-dependency-check-requires.t has the tripwire: its last subtest asserts Cmd::Create still has no ->json, and the requires-coverage subtest asserts json is the only undeclared call left. Both fail when this is fixed, which is the reminder to move json up into the requires line.
Split done. Role::DependencyCheck keeps the report-time half (check_dependencies, dependency_report, _dependency_warnings) and now declares requires qw( store find_task json quiet ) -- json included, which was the point. New Role::DependencyArgs holds the set-time half (parse_dependency_ids, assert_dependencies_exist) with requires qw( find_task usage_error ). Wiring: Create composes DependencyArgs only (no longer inherits the reporting half), Edit adds DependencyArgs next to TaskMutation, Pick and TaskMutation are unchanged -- the ticket expected their with-lines to move, but with the reporting half keeping the DependencyCheck name they do not. t/135 pulled forward: both tripwires replaced by the new promise (each role declares every call it makes, nothing undeclared; create has no reporting half at all). New t/140-dependency-role-split.t asserts the halves are disjoint and which consumer gets which. t/77 MutationConsumer now composes Role::Output, which it always needed for run_batch's $self->json. Test: prove -l t/135-dependency-check-requires.t t/140-dependency-role-split.t -> PASS; full prove -l -j4 t/ -> 131 files, 953 tests, PASS. Not committed, Changes untouched.
